    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=50,\\ y=20$.\n\nCombine the logarithms to obtain $xy=1000$, then substitute $x=y+30$ and retain the positive solution.",
      "worked": "The original logarithms require $x>0$ and $y>0$. Combining them gives $\\log_{10}(xy)=3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}xy&=10^3\\\\xy&=1000\\\\x&=y+30\\\\y(y+30)&=1000\\\\y^2+30y-1000&=0\\\\(y+50)(y-20)&=0\\\\y&=-50\\text{ or }20.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $y>0$, retain $y=20$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=20+30\\\\x&=50.\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values are positive, $50-20=30$, and $\\log_{10}(50)+\\log_{10}(20)=\\log_{10}(1000)=3$. Hence $x=50$ and $y=20$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
